From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 16:13:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tick the entity tracker in parallel region buckets

The tracker was the largest serial section left in the world tick:
one flat loop running range math and dirty-data sync for every
tracked entity times every nearby player. Bucket it by region cell
exactly like parallel entity ticking. Workers evaluate visibility and
send dirty data (packet sends are thread-safe enqueues); a pairing
transition - the rare case - routes to the owning thread through the
region mailbox, because pairing fires a cancellable event whose veto
must gate the mutation synchronously, and because a worker must not
push overlapping single-chunk leases. The steady state where a pair
stays visible or stays hidden mutates nothing and is answered by the
worker with pure math.

The visibility decision is extracted unchanged into a helper shared
by both paths, so serial behavior is byte-identical.

